{number: 16}
{title: Fairest Lord Jesus}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Fairest Lord [Bb] Jesus, [Eb] Ruler of [Ab] all [Eb] nature,
[Eb] O Thou of [Ab] God and [Eb] man the [Bb] Son,
[Eb] Thee will I [Ab] cherish, [Eb] Thee will I [Bb] honor,
[Cm] Thou, my soul's [Ab] glory, [Eb] joy, [Bb] and [Eb] crown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Fair are the [Bb] meadows, [Eb] fairer still the [Ab] wood-[Eb] lands,
[Eb] Robed in the [Ab] blooming [Eb] garb of [Bb] spring:
[Eb] Jesus is [Ab] fairer, [Eb] Jesus is [Bb] purer,
[Cm] Who makes the [Ab] woeful [Eb] heart [Bb] to [Eb] sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Fair is the [Bb] sunshine, [Eb] fairer still the [Ab] moon-[Eb] light,
[Eb] And all the [Ab] twinkling, [Eb] starry [Bb] host:
[Eb] Jesus shines [Ab] brighter, [Eb] Jesus shines [Bb] purer,
[Cm] Than all the [Ab] angels [Eb] heaven [Bb] can [Eb] boast.
{end_of_verse}
